    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0858" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/1–2047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Nicaragua
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-22T15:00:00-05:00">January 22, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Urtel 25 Jan 20.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d719-f1"/> Were Embassy to comply with President Somoza’s request,
                    it would be acting as intermediary between him and opposition, a procedure which
                    Dept has considered undesirable. No objection is perceived, however, to your
                    confirming facts if inquiry is made by opposition leaders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d719-f1" n="5" xml:id="d719-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; Ambassador Warren reported that he had conveyed orally to President
                    Somoza the substance of Department’s telegram 12 of January 18, and the latter
                    had asked that Ambassador Warren let General Chamorro and others know of his
                    request to the Department and its refusal (817.00/1–2047).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
